course: dictionary
lesson: 576
title: Who is an author?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An author is a person who writes a book, story, poem or article. You can usually find the author's name on the cover of a book. «Authors choose every word on purpose.» That means a writer picks each word for a reason.
explain: The word author has another meaning too. The author of a plan, idea or event is the person who started or created it. So when someone asks who the author of an idea is, they want to know who thought it up first.
explain: Read like a writer by asking two questions. What is the author's purpose: to entertain, to inform or to persuade? How does the author make you feel? The answers are in the words, sentences and tricks the author uses.
fact: An author is a person who writes a book, story, poem or article.
fact: To author something means to write it. This verb is formal, so you will mostly see it in serious writing.
fact: Famous children's authors include Roald Dahl, J.K. Rowling, Dr Seuss, Beverly Cleary and Mem Fox.
fact: «An author's choice is a decision about words, sentences or layout, made on purpose.»
fact: Useful phrases are «the author of», «a famous author», «author's purpose» and «author visit».
exercise: What is an author? | A person who sells books in a shop | A person who reads books aloud in a library | *A person who writes a book, story, poem or article | A person who draws the pictures in a book
exercise: «Authors choose every word on purpose.» What does this sentence tell you? | Words are picked by chance | Only poems have chosen words | Authors never think about their words | *Writers pick each word for a reason
exercise: «Authors sometimes break the usual pattern to surprise the reader.» Why might an author do this? | To stop people from reading it | To make the book shorter | *To surprise the reader | To copy another book
test: Who is the author of a book? | *The person who wrote it | The person who sold it in a shop | The person who printed it | The person who bought it
test: «Reading like a writer means noticing the tricks an author uses, not just what happens.» What should a reader notice? | *The tricks an author uses | The colour of the cover | Only the names of the characters | The price printed on the cover
exam: What does it mean to author something? | To read it aloud | To sell it | To print it | *To write it
